# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Xcode
#
# `project.xcworkspace/` is regenerated by Xcode on every open, and carries
# per-developer state. `xcshareddata/` is deliberately NOT ignored: the shared
# scheme lives there and CI builds with it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
DerivedData/
*.xcactivitylog
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
*.xccheckout
*.xcscmblueprint
*.moved-aside
*.hmap
*.ipa
*.dSYM
*.dSYM.zip
KagiPeek.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Swift Package Manager
#
# `Package.resolved` is intentionally not listed. This package has no external
# dependencies today, so nothing is generated; if it ever gains any, the lock
# file belongs in the repository so a build is reproducible. Ignore it only
# over a deliberate decision, not by habit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.build/
.swiftpm/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release artifacts
#
# Notarisation zips and disk images are produced under build/ as well; these
# catch the ones written elsewhere.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
*.dmg
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials and key material
#
# Nothing of the kind is committed today — signing reads the keychain and the
# scripts take identities and notary profiles from the environment. These rules
# exist so that a certificate dropped at the root is refused by default rather
# than pushed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.local
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.xcconfig.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
.cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and tools
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
# Atomic-save scratch files. An editor that writes through a temporary (`.!12345!File.swift`,
# `.#File.swift`) leaves one behind whenever it is interrupted, and because the name keeps the
# `.swift` extension it is picked up by `find KagiPeek -name '*.swift'` and compiled as a second
# copy of the same type. One such file reached a commit on 2026-11-05.
.!*
.#*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Merge leftovers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.orig
*.rej
*.patch

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working papers
#
# Point-in-time engineering reports. They go stale the moment the code moves,
# and `docs/` is where anything meant to be read later lives. Kept on disk,
# out of the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
deliverables/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WorkBuddy working data
#
# Session memory and notes for this workspace. Local by nature: it records what
# was done here, not what the project is. (Not deleted — only untracked.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.workbuddy/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QwenWork session workspace
#
# Scratch area for QwenWork desktop sessions: canvas previews, review reports
# and backup patches. Local by nature, like .workbuddy/ — it records what
# happened in a session, not what the project is.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
qwenwork/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZCode agent session data
#
# Plans and session state for ZCode CLI runs in this workspace, like .workbuddy/
# and qwenwork/ above: local working data, not part of the project.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.zcode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent workspace
#
# Local plans, specs and MCP configuration for the coding agent. Session data
# by nature, like .workbuddy/ and .zcode/ above — it records how the work was
# planned, not what the project is.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.trae/
